                        "entry_id": "3543d99c-eb68-318d-b89f-b6eaf818628e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The act of one who bewails something."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4372c7f2-a78e-455a-8fab-27477e8f7980",
                                "sense_id": "e6069a8c-a5be-3377-a353-b0b64d55ff7e",
                                "text": "We might have been!—these are but common words,\nAnd yet they make the sum of life's bewailing;\nThey are the echo of those finer chords,\nWhose music life deplores when unavailing,\nWe might have been!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "03da4ab9-1e88-4910-8da7-b31631fac917",
                                "sense_id": "e6069a8c-a5be-3377-a353-b0b64d55ff7e",
                                "text": "No suggestions, no words, no bewailings could improve it. Still it was very human to make suggestions, and utter words, and make piteous bewailings over and over again."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
